    "body": "\n# Description\n\nNVFP4 columnwise RHT on SM120/SM121 fails with `Assertion failed: rht_matrix != nullptr. Columnwise RHT requires an RHT matrix.` The scale-type dispatch wrapper introduced in #3325 accepts `rht_matrix` but passes `nullptr` to `quantize_transpose_impl`, discarding the valid matrix\nprovided by the SM120/SM121 path added in #3300.\n\nForward `rht_matrix` through the wrapper so columnwise RHT receives the supplied matrix. Calls that omit the optional argument continue to pass `nullptr`.\n\nRelated: #3062. This fixes the dropped-argument regression in #3325; the original shared-memory issue described in #3062 has a different cause.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [ ] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\n- [ ] Code refactoring\n\n## Changes\n\n- Forward the caller's RHT matrix to `quantize_transpose_impl` for both NVFP4 scale types.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n- [x] The functionality is complete\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas (no additional comments needed)\n- [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (not applicable; restores existing behavior)\n- [ ] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [ ] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works (covered by the existing `tests/pytorch/nvfp4/test_nvfp4_rht_sm12x.py`)\n- [ ] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\n\n<!-- Local draft only. GPU tests have not been run in this macOS checkout.\nHuman author review is required before requesting maintainer review. -->",
