      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=79088561\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n**[Medium impact]** The change appears safe to merge and restores the intended columnwise RHT call.\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nForwards `rht_matrix` through the NVFP4 scale-type switch instead of replacing it with `nullptr`.\n- NVFP4 columnwise RHT receives its supplied matrix.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Forward the RHT matrix in NVFP4 quantize...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/fb98b935d6054a2fc68137951051695de3acaee3) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_expert&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=code_reviews&utm_content=nvidia/transformerengine)</sub>",
